      "problem": "Solve for $x$, where $\\dfrac{6-2x}{2} = \\dfrac{6-x}{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6-2x}{2} & =\\frac{6-x}{3} \\\\ (6-2x)\\cdot 3 & =2\\cdot (6-x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we proceed as usual to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6-2x)\\cdot 3 & =2\\cdot (6-x) \\\\ 18-6x & =12-2x \\\\ 18-6x-18 & =12-2x-18 \\\\ -6x & =-2x-6 \\\\ -6x+2x & =-2x-6+2x \\\\ -4x & =-6 \\\\ \\frac{-4x}{-4} & =\\frac{-6}{-4} \\\\ x & =\\frac{6}{4} \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
